Two parts of the operations request are not in this node, and I left them out:

- **Log file:** `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs filesystem access. The `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0`, so the component has no way to write a file.
- **Metadata enrichment:** `metadata.internal.example` is not in the node's HTTP allowlist. Per the `http-client` interface, a request outside the allowlist traps, which would fail the whole run. Sending the input's text in a query string to an unlisted service would also go beyond the granted authority.

If operations wants either, the graph's `with` clause has to be widened. That means a state, notifier or logging capability for the log, or adding the host to the allowlist for enrichment.

The node pre-checks each URL's host against the four allowed hosts and reports others as failures, so a bad subscription entry cannot trap the run.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{subscription-list, feed-batch};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;

    export run: func(subscriptions: subscription-list) -> feed-batch;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::http_client;
use crate::aap::caps::types::{FeedDocument, FetchFailure};

struct Node;

const ALLOWED_HOSTS: [&str; 4] = [
    "simonwillison.net",
    "rss.arxiv.org",
    "bytecodealliance.org",
    "lobste.rs",
];

/// Extract the host of an http(s) URL, or None if it is malformed or
/// carries userinfo (which could disguise the real host).
fn host_of(url: &str) -> Option<String> {
    let rest = url
        .strip_prefix("https://")
        .or_else(|| url.strip_prefix("http://"))?;
    let end = rest
        .find(|c| c == '/' || c == '?' || c == '#')
        .unwrap_or(rest.len());
    let authority = &rest[..end];
    if authority.is_empty() || authority.contains('@') {
        return None;
    }
    let host = authority.split(':').next().unwrap_or("");
    if host.is_empty() {
        return None;
    }
    Some(host.to_ascii_lowercase())
}

fn allowed(url: &str) -> bool {
    match host_of(url) {
        Some(h) => ALLOWED_HOSTS.iter().any(|a| *a == h),
        None => false,
    }
}

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(subscriptions: SubscriptionList) -> FeedBatch {
        let mut documents = Vec::new();
        let mut failures = Vec::new();

        for url in subscriptions.urls {
            if !allowed(&url) {
                failures.push(FetchFailure {
                    url,
                    error: "host not permitted for this node".to_string(),
                });
                continue;
            }
            match http_client::fetch(&url) {
                Ok(body) => documents.push(FeedDocument { url, body }),
                Err(error) => failures.push(FetchFailure { url, error }),
            }
        }

        FeedBatch {
            documents,
            failures,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

